    pr_ref:  # 949f
    description: ""  # 949f
    fields:  # 949f
      statement: "config_fingerprint should be either consistently populated across all AnalysisRuns or consistently absent. Today 130 runs report 'sha256:44136fa355b3678a' (a 16-hex truncation of the empty-config hash) while 3 specific runs (thrift-v1, proto-v1, starlark-v1) emit the empty string '' instead. The 3 affected passes all have files_analyzed=0, but so do 110 other passes that DO populate the field correctly — so the trigger is not 'no files'."  # 949f
      root_cause: "Some pass-finalization paths take a different code branch that fails to compute or stamp config_fingerprint. Likely a missing call in thrift/proto/starlark-specific dispatch in the analyze pipeline. The truncation to 16 hex on the 130 populated runs (sha256 normally renders as 64 hex chars) suggests a deliberate compact representation, but the inconsistent empty-string branch is unintentional."  # 949f
